<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>index on Khalid9ASSI</title><link>https://khalid9assi.com/</link><description>Recent content in index on Khalid9ASSI</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 09 May 2026 14:30:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://khalid9assi.com/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Neuroplasticity</title><link>https://khalid9assi.com/posts/neuroplasticity/</link><pubDate>Sat, 09 May 2026 14:30:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://khalid9assi.com/posts/neuroplasticity/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Neuroplasticity&lt;/strong&gt; is the brain&amp;rsquo;s lifelong capacity to reorganize itself by forming, strengthening, or pruning neural connections in response to experience, learning, and environment. It&amp;rsquo;s not a metaphor, it&amp;rsquo;s a literal physical restructuring of brain tissue.&lt;/p&gt;














 





 




 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 









 










 








 




&lt;div style="background-color: #fff; padding: 1rem 0;"&gt;
 &lt;img src="https://khalid9assi.com/imgs/neurplasticity-graph.png"
 style="width: 986px; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; height: auto" alt="Analytics"loading="lazy"
 &gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The three mechanisms are :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synaptogenesis : building new synaptic connections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pruning : eliminating pathways you don&amp;rsquo;t use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Myelination : brain wraps the pathways you use most in a protective layer, making signals travel faster. The more you repeat something, the quicker and smoother that connection becomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to drive neuroplasticity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>TWIL 19 2026</title><link>https://khalid9assi.com/twil/19-2026/</link><pubDate>Sat, 09 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://khalid9assi.com/twil/19-2026/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Neuroplasticity&lt;/strong&gt; :
